            "level": {
                "value": 5
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Fear eaters are malicious fey who revel in causing fear in mortals, using it to grow strange, glowing mushrooms from the bodies of their terrified victims. While they require no sustenance to live, fear eaters consider these emotion-soaked mushrooms to be delicacies of the highest order. A few have established \"farms\" in remote corners of the First World, where they hold kidnapped mortals captive and regularly harvest their fears, discreetly selling their produce to influential fey.</p>\n<p>A fear eater resembles a grotesque caterpillar, lined with several pairs of arms and many stubby legs. They can be found in a variety of colors, and some exhibit iridescent patterns across their elongated torsos, dyed by consumption of their colorful crop. A fear eater almost always carries a hookah bowl strapped to their side or back, from which they continually take deep lungfuls of a miasma made from spores of their fear mushrooms.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
        },
